# @@NAME@@ agent notes

This is a standalone @@DIMENSION@@ game. Its only direct dependency is the local
`ferravex` facade; keep the entire dependency graph first-party/std-only.

- Read `README.md`, `src/game.rs` and `src/lib.rs` before changing gameplay.
- Keep fixed simulation in `Game::advance`; use `GameSession` for lifecycle and
  timing. `Game::TICK_RATE_HZ` is the configured rate; keep it finite and in
  `1..=1000`. Restart must reset both interpolation poses and the clock.
- Sample `PlayerInput::sample` once per rendered frame. Handle global menu
  actions there; apply held movement for every fixed step. For added gameplay
  buttons, consume `PlayerInput::pressed`/`take` inside actual fixed ticks and
  pass values to the rules. Preserve edges on zero-tick frames and consume them
  once across catch-up ticks. Draw using the returned interpolation alpha.
- This single-player session pauses for local menus. For network/replay games,
  keep the authoritative clock running while local menus suppress commands.
- Keep `ferravex::render::game!`, the native launcher and the browser ABI intact.
- Add behavioral regression tests for rule changes and document public APIs
  with compiling rustdoc examples.
- Run `cargo test --offline --locked --jobs 2`; build the browser with
  `python3 -B scripts/build-web.py`. Do not edit generated `target/` output.
- `Cargo.toml` and `ferravex.json` point to the engine checkout. Treat engine
  source as a dependency; project changes should stay in this game.
- `ferravex.json` schema version 1 records generation options and generated file
  paths. Its tick rate/title are provenance, not live settings. Read README's
  customization section before editing them; changing metadata alone does not
  change `Game::TICK_RATE_HZ`, Rust window configuration or browser titles.
- Inspect the local facade/engine implementation before adopting an API. The
  generated game uses `GameSession::new/start/toggle_pause/restart/advance`,
  `PlayerInput::preset/sample/movement/pressed/simulation_dt`,
  `render::window_conf`, and `render::game!`; do not assume planned APIs exist.
- Do not add registry/Git crates, third-party JS, CDN loaders, or silently
  change protocols/save formats. No workspace/catalog edits or deployment are
  needed to run this project.
